    "Reason : 1 - The inclusion of a rear access and primary living accommodation within the outbuilding renders the use of the outbuilding as non-incidental to the enjoyment of the main dwellinghouse which would be considered inappropriate development. In addition, the design of the porch is unacceptable due to the design adjoining the bay window that is present on the front elevation. These design choices result in a proposal that fails to comply with requirements laid out in Local Plan Policies SC7, CC1, CC2 and the aims and objectives of the Residential Extension Guidelines "
